id: pm-q5iao5
title: "Fold pm package explore, inventory and manage into one installed-package listing with --depth brief|standard|deep, and align the SDK list target and the MCP package tool with it"
description: "Follow-up to pm-gh1777, which made pm package list an alias of the static inventory, gave every listing one --fields contract and dropped contributions from default explore/manage rows. Three listings of the same installed set remain, with different costs and evidence: inventory (static, offline, last observed update), explore (runtime-probed activation) and manage (runtime probe plus a live registry check that records update observations). The report's third suggestion was one command with --depth brief|standard|deep, as pm context does: brief = inventory rows, standard = explore activation status, deep = manage freshness. Two inconsistencies to settle in the same change: the SDK runExtension positional target list still maps to explore (src/sdk/extension.ts IMPLICIT_EXTENSION_ACTIONS), while the CLI list subcommand is the inventory; and the MCP pm_package tool exposes catalog/explore/manage but no inventory action (PM_EXTENSION_PACKAGE_ACTION_SUBCOMMANDS). Keep explore and manage as compatibility spellings. Duplicate check: searched fold package explore inventory manage depth listing; no open owner."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 3
tags[5]: agent-ux,consolidation,extensions,packages,token-efficiency
